INT. COACHING INN STABLE LOFT, ENGLAND - NIGHT, 1788

Hay. Lantern light. The smell of horse and rain. A rope ladder to the yard below.

A cloaked figure crouches in the straw, back to the wall, pistol held in both hands.

The ladder creaks.

LADY GEORGIANA ASHWORTH-OLUWOLE (30s, riding habit torn at the hem, hair coming loose) climbs into the loft and freezes at the sight of the pistol.

GEORGIANA
Put that away, please.

STRANGER
Stay where you are.

GEORGIANA
I have been riding for nine hours. I will sit.

She sits on a hay bale. The stranger does not lower the pistol.

STRANGER
Who sent you?

GEORGIANA
Nobody. I own the horse in the third stall. I came to check on her.

STRANGER
Liar.

GEORGIANA
I assure you, I am not.

The stranger leans out of shadow. A man, late twenties, rain-soaked, hollow-eyed, in the coat of a courier.

STRANGER (CONT'D)
The horse in the third stall is mine.

GEORGIANA
It is a grey mare with a white sock?

STRANGER
(beat)
A brown gelding.

GEORGIANA
Then we are both mistaken.

She smiles, tilts her head, and the tension shifts, just slightly. He lowers the pistol an inch.

STRANGER
I am a courier. I carry letters for the Crown.

GEORGIANA
How dull.

STRANGER
You'd be surprised.

GEORGIANA
Show me one.

STRANGER
No.

GEORGIANA
Then tell me your name, courier.

He hesitates, searching her face for a lie.

STRANGER
Matthias.

GEORGIANA
Matthias what?

MATTHIAS
Just Matthias.

GEORGIANA
Then call me Georgiana. Just Georgiana.

The ladder creaks again. Both turn. Boots on the rungs. Torchlight on the beams.

A VOICE (O.S.)
(from below)
Search the loft!

Matthias grabs her arm. She grabs his wrist. They freeze, nose to nose, as torchlight crawls along the straw.

MATTHIAS
(whispering)
They've come for me.

GEORGIANA
Then they shall have us both.

MATTHIAS
Why?

GEORGIANA
Because I'm tired of being polite.

She yanks him down into the hay. Pulls her cloak over them both. Torchlight sweeps over the rafters. A soldier's head appears at the top of the ladder, squinting.

SOLDIER (O.S.)
Nothing here.

SOLDIER (CONT'D)
(calling)
Only straw and horse-dung!

The head vanishes. Boots descend. Silence returns.

Matthias and Georgiana lie breathless beneath the cloak.

GEORGIANA
(whispering)
You're heavier than you look.

MATTHIAS
You're braver than you look.

GEORGIANA
We are both liars.

MATTHIAS
Obviously.

They begin, helplessly, to laugh. Then to shake. Then, finally, to lie very still, listening to the rain on the slates.

Matthias slides the pistol into his belt.

MATTHIAS (CONT'D)
(to the room)
I owe you.

GEORGIANA
(to him)
I'll collect.
